{"name":"Peacock House","hex":"#2e4b44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peacock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male peafowl, especially Pavo cristatus, notable for its brilliant iridescently ocellated tail.","A peafowl (of the genus Pavo or Afropavo), either male or female."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strut about proudly or haughtily.","To engage in peacocking, ostentatious dress or behaviour to impress women."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peacock"},{"term":"house","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A structure built or serving as an abode of human beings. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An apartment building within a public housing estate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To keep within a structure or container.","To admit to residence; to harbor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/house"}],"entries":[{"title":"Debenham House","blocks":[{"text":"Debenham House at 8 Addison Road is a large detached house in the Holland Park district of Kensington and Chelsea, W14. Built in the Arts and Crafts style by the architect Halsey Ricardo, it is a Grade I listed building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Debenham_House_%2835482927182%29.jpg/330px-Debenham_House_%2835482927182%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debenham_House","wikidata":"Q5248061"},{"title":"Peafowl","blocks":[{"text":"Peafowl is a common name for two bird species of the genus Pavo and one species of the closely related genus Afropavo within the tribe Pavonini of the family Phasianidae. Male peafowl are referred to as peacocks, and female peafowl are referred to as peahens. Despite this, peacock is usually used to refer to both sexes, in common language."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Peacock_Plumage.jpg/330px-Peacock_Plumage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peafowl","wikidata":"Q201251"},{"title":"House","blocks":[{"text":"A house is a residential building. It may range in complexity from a rudimentary hut to a complex structure of wood, masonry, concrete or other material, outfitted with plumbing, electrical, and heating, ventilation, and air conditioning systems. Houses use a range of different roofing systems to keep precipitation such as rain from getting into the dwelling space. Houses generally have doors or locks to secure the dwelling space and protect its inhabitants and contents from burglars or other trespassers. Most conventional modern houses in Western cultures will contain one or more bedrooms and bathrooms, a kitchen or cooking area, and a living room. A house may have a separate dining room, or the eating area may be integrated into the kitchen or another room. Some large houses in North America have a recreation room. In traditional agriculture-oriented societies, domestic animals such as chickens or larger livestock may share part of the house with humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg/330px-Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House","wikidata":"Q3947"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg/500px-Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg/500px-Eggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEggs_of_Peafowl_at_Aravath_Kasaragod.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wi